      "currency": "GBP",
      "description": "Are you walking more or less than usual today? One glance at your wrist answers it.\n\nOn Pace draws the comparison you know from the Health app (today so far against your average day) and puts it where you actually look: on your Apple Watch face and on your iPhone Home Screen.\n\nTHE GRAPH, ON YOUR WATCH FACE\nAn orange line for today, a grey line for your average, and the two numbers that matter. It fits the large rectangular slot of Modular and Infograph Modular, and the Smart Stack. Smaller slots show how far along your usual pace you are.\n\nTHE SAME NUMBERS AS THE HEALTH APP\nThe day graph averages the previous four weeks, hour by hour, exactly as Health does. What you see on your wrist matches what you see in Health.\n\nDAY, WEEK, MONTH AND YEAR\nThis week against your usual week. This month against your usual month. This year against the years before it.\n\nLIKE WITH LIKE\nMondays are not Saturdays. Compare today with the same day of the week, or this November with your other Novembers.\n\nBARS, TOO\nHours of today, the last seven days, the last twelve weeks or months, side by side with their average.\n\nNOT ONLY STEPS\nDistance, active energy and flights climbed get the same graphs. If you use a wheelchair, it counts pushes and wheelchair distance instead.\n\nWIDGETS ON IPHONE\nHome Screen and Lock Screen widgets with the same comparison.\n\nPRIVATE BY DESIGN\nOn Pace reads your activity from Apple Health, with your permission, and never writes to it. Your data stays on your iPhone and your Apple Watch. No account, no servers, no analytics, no ads.\n\nApple Watch is optional: the iPhone app and widgets work on their own.",
